---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  appName="Legal"
  docTitle="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the apps of Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho, BSc handle your data, and the rights you have."
  canonicalUrl="https://rubenspessoa.dev/privacy/"
  effectiveDate="July 23, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers all apps published by Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho, BSc, operating under the
    business name &ldquo;Pixeldog&rdquo; (&ldquo;we&rdquo;), their websites, and this website. It
    explains what data is processed, why, who processes it, and the rights you have. It is written
    to apply to every app we publish, so depending on which app you use, only a subset of it
    applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    The short version: our apps are designed to work without accounts, your content stays on your
    device (and in your own iCloud, if you use it), payments run through Apple, and we do not sell
    your personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Rubens Pessoa de Barros Filho, BSc (Pixeldog)
    <br />
    UNESCO-Esplanade 8/55, 8020 Graz, Austria
    <br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a> for full legal details.
  </p>

  <h2>What we process</h2>
  <p>
    What is processed depends on the features of the app you use. Across our apps, processing falls
    into these categories:
  </p>

  <h3>AI features</h3>
  <p>
    In apps with AI features, the content you submit for processing &mdash; photos, text, uploaded
    documents, or text transcribed from voice input &mdash; is sent through our servers to
    third-party AI providers, solely to generate the result. This content carries no account
    identifier, is not used to train AI models under our API agreements, and is not stored on our
    servers: it is processed in memory and discarded.
  </p>

  <h3>Your content</h3>
  <p>
    The content you create in our apps &mdash; saved photos, chat history, habits, notes, and
    similar &mdash; is stored on your device and, if you use iCloud, synced through your own private
    iCloud storage. We run no accounts and keep no copy on our servers.
  </p>

  <h3>Anonymous identifiers</h3>
  <p>
    Apps that talk to our servers create an anonymous identifier via Firebase to enforce fair usage
    limits and connect a subscription to your installation, and may verify requests with Firebase
    App Check to keep bots away. We cannot identify you personally from these identifiers.
  </p>

  <h3>Location</h3>
  <p>
    In apps with location-based features, and only with your permission, your device location is
    used at query time to show nearby results. It is not stored as a movement history.
  </p>

  <h3>Ads and attribution</h3>
  <p>
    In apps with a free ad-supported tier, ads are served by Google AdMob: if you allow tracking in
    the iOS App Tracking Transparency prompt, ads may be personalized; if you decline, they are not.
    Attribution services (such as AppsFlyer or Adjust) process device identifiers to attribute app
    installs to marketing campaigns, subject to the same tracking choice.
  </p>

  <h3>Analytics and crash reporting</h3>
  <p>
    Our apps may collect analytics events about feature usage &mdash; not the content you create
    &mdash; and crash reports (device model, OS version, crash traces) to keep the apps working
    well.
  </p>

  <h3>This website and app websites</h3>
  <p>
    This website (rubenspessoa.dev) is static and sets no cookies and runs no analytics. Some app
    websites use analytics and, where required, ask for cookie consent; their processing is covered
    by the services listed below.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    We keep the list of processors as small as each app allows. Not every service is used by every
    app &mdash; which subset applies depends on the app&rsquo;s features. Contact us for
    app-specific details:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Apple (USA): App Store distribution, payments, device services, iCloud</li>
    <li>
      Google Firebase (USA/Ireland): server infrastructure (Cloud Functions), app verification (App
      Check), analytics (Google Analytics for Firebase), and crash reporting (Crashlytics)
    </li>
    <li>RevenueCat (USA): subscription status, keyed to anonymous identifiers</li>
    <li>OpenAI (USA) and Anthropic (USA): generating AI responses</li>
    <li>Other specialized AI service providers (USA): AI analysis of submitted photos</li>
    <li>PostHog (EU-hosted): product analytics</li>
    <li>TelemetryDeck (Germany): anonymized product analytics</li>
    <li>Amplitude (USA): product analytics</li>
    <li>Sentry (USA): crash and error reporting</li>
    <li>Google AdMob (USA): advertising in free ad-supported tiers</li>
    <li>AppsFlyer (USA/EU) and Adjust (Germany): install attribution</li>
    <li>Algolia (USA): search features</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR (and the corresponding bases of the Brazilian LGPD) we process data based on:{' '}
    <strong>performance of a contract</strong> (providing the app features you use and your
    subscription), <strong>legitimate interest</strong> (product analytics, crash reporting, abuse
    prevention, non-personalized ads), <strong>consent</strong> (location access, personalized
    advertising, tracking-based attribution), and <strong>legal obligation</strong> where
    applicable.
  </p>

  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Where providers are located in the USA or other countries outside the EU, transfers rely on the
    EU-US Data Privacy Framework, Standard Contractual Clauses, or equivalent safeguards (including
    those recognized by the LGPD for users in Brazil).
  </p>

  <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data is processed and stored only as long as required by the purpose it was collected
    for: content submitted to AI features is not retained on our servers at all; rate-limit and
    usage counters expire automatically within days; analytics, attribution, and crash data follow
    the retention settings of the respective tool. Once the retention period expires, data is
    deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you have the right to access, rectify, delete, restrict, or receive
    a copy of your data, to object to processing based on legitimate interest, and to withdraw
    consent at any time (for tracking and location, directly in iOS Settings).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>EU/EEA and Switzerland:</strong> the rights above under the GDPR and Swiss FADP, and
      the right to complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (
      <a href="https://www.dsb.gv.at" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        dsb.gv.at
      </a>
      ) or your local supervisory authority.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Brazil:</strong> the rights of the LGPD, including confirmation of processing,
      anonymization or elimination of unnecessary data, information about sharing, review of
      automated decisions, and the right to complain to the ANPD.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>United States:</strong> where state privacy laws apply, the right to know, correct,
      delete, and port your data, to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information and of
      targeted advertising, and to non-discrimination for exercising these rights. The tracking
      consent in iOS Settings is the most direct opt-out for ad-related sharing.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Because we hold no account for you, exercising these rights works by email: write to{' '}
    <a href="mailto:contact@rubenspessoa.dev">contact@rubenspessoa.dev</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our apps are not directed at children under 14 (or under 13 in the United States), and we do not
    knowingly collect data from them. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we
    will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we will update it here with a new effective date and, as far as
    technically and legally feasible, notify you in the affected app. Where changes affect
    processing based on your consent, we will collect new consent where required.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
